If a clinician does not provably understand a methadone-risk-profile then it is recommended that the clinician does not consider a methadone-treatment for a pain.
If a clinician does not provably prepare a patient-education then it is recommended that the clinician does not consider a methadone-treatment for a pain.
If a clinician does not provably prepare a close-patient-monitoring then it is recommended that the clinician does not consider a methadone-treatment for a pain.
If a clinician does not provably assess a QT-prolongation-risk then it is recommended that the clinician does not consider a methadone-treatment for a pain.
If a clinician does not provably consider an electrocardiographic-monitoring then it is recommended that the clinician does not consider a methadone-treatment for a pain.
